   "id": "rosh_hashanah.30a.15",
   "daf": "30a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "שׁוֹמַעַת — פְּרָט לְיוֹשֶׁבֶת בְּרֹאשׁ הָהָר. קְרוֹבָה — פְּרָט לְיוֹשֶׁבֶת חוּץ לַתְּחוּם. וִיכוֹלָה לָבוֹא — פְּרָט לְמַפְסֵיק לַהּ נַהֲרָא.",
   "en": "When the mishna states that the city must be able to «hear,» this serves to «exclude» a city «sitting on a mountaintop,» from where one can see Jerusalem but cannot hear sounds from it. As for the requirement that the city must be «near,» this comes to «exclude» a place «sitting beyond» the Shabbat «limit» of Jerusalem, even if one can see and hear from that place. «And» with regard to the statement that one «can come,» this serves to «exclude» a city «that is separated» from Jerusalem «by a river,» which renders it impossible for people to come to the city, even if it is close by."
  }
 ],
